-- title:
--   Orbits of cyclic N-subgroups count moduli points over j(E₀)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number and let $E_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the ambient field is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) which is elliptic. On the left-hand side one considers the type [`ModularCurve.CycSub E₀ N`](def/ModularCurve_EMD.html#L36) of those additive subgroups $H$ of the affine point group $E_0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ for which there exists a point $g$ of additive order exactly $N$ with $H$ the subgroup of integer multiples of $g$, and one forms the quotient (in the sense of `Quot`, i.e. by the equivalence relation generated by the given relation) of this type by the relation [`ModularCurve.SameOrbit E₀`](def/ModularCurve_EMD.html#L40) applied to the underlying subgroups: $H$ and $H'$ are so related when there is a variable change $\gamma$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing $E_0$, i.e. $\gamma \bullet E_0 = E_0$, and there are points $g, g'$ with $H$ the multiples of $g$, $H'$ the multiples of $g'$, and $g'$ heterogeneously equal to the image of $g$ under the transport `Point.vcInvFun` along $\gamma$. On the right-hand side one considers the set of $x$ in [`ModularCurve.ModuliPoint N (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`](def/ModularCurve_ModuliPoint.html#L35) — the quotient of the type of triples (an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a point `gen` of additive order $N$) by the relation that $P$ and $Q$ are related when some variable change $\gamma$ carries $P$'s curve to $Q$'s curve and $Q$'s generator is, heterogeneously, $k$ times the transport of $P$'s generator along $\gamma$ for some natural $k$ coprime to $N$ — subject to the condition that the induced $j$-invariant `ModuliPoint.j x` equals $j(E_0)$. The assertion is that these two types have equal `Nat.card`.
--
--   This is the moduli-theoretic count of points of $X_0(N)$ lying over a fixed $j$-invariant: the $\mathrm{Aut}(E_0)$-orbits of cyclic subgroups of order $N$ in $E_0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ are equinumerous with the pairs $(E,C)$ whose underlying curve has $j(E) = j(E_0)$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.card_eq_natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq_of_EMD`](thm.html#ModularCurve.card_eq_natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq_of_EMD), and its proof goes through [`ModularCurve.natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq_eq_natCard_quot_addOrderOf_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq_eq_natCard_quot_addOrderOf_eq), which replaces the right-hand side by a quotient of the set of points of exact order $N$ on $E_0$, together with the additivity of the transport map [`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.vcInvFun`](def/WeierstrassCurve_VariableChangePointEquiv.html#L119).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_natCard_quot_sameOrbit_cycSub_eq_natCard_moduliPoint_j_eq.lean

import Mathlib
